  "editorial_note": "GitHub listed thirteen projects this Friday morning, and five of them were featured here in the past week. Today's six picks are all first appearances: Alibaba's Qwen Code, which ==opened a 1.0 Preview this week==, TensorFold's Zig-built inference server, a proxy that ==points Claude Code and other agent harnesses at other providers' models==, llama.cpp's fresh v0.9.0, the long-lived nvm, and an Apple Watch curiosity. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
  "coverage_notes": [
    "GitHub's daily listing held 13 rows at capture. The capture parsed exactly thirteen listing rows and is GitHub's own list, not a truncation by us.",
    "All 13 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata was checked at about 07:01:30 UTC for the candidates, and recent releases for every entry; README files of the six picks were read at about 07:01:45 UTC. Every checked repository was active and unarchived.",
    "Five entries featured in the past seven days were left out without a new primary-sourced reason: meta/astryx (8 November), addyosmani/agent-skills and we-promise/sure (11 November), and GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src and openai/codex-security (12 November).",
    "meta/astryx shipped v0.7.15 and we-promise/sure a v0.7.6 hotfix since their picks; we did not judge either a material change. openai/codex-security has no release since the 0.10.0 covered yesterday.",
    "nodejs/node (picked 24 October) and CopilotKit/OpenBot (picked 30 October) were also on the list; they fall outside the seven-day window but were not re-featured without a new reason.",
    "The preceding seven calendar dates, 6-12 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
    "The official listing was captured at 08:01:10 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
    "Feature descriptions, token allowances and performance figures come from each project's own README and release notes and are the maintainers' claims. No candidate code, installer, CLI, app or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
  ],
