      ],
      "description": "Qwen Code is an open-source AI coding agent for the terminal, with IDE plugins, a desktop app, a web UI, SDKs and chat integrations. The README lists memory, skills, sub-agents, agent teams and MCP support, and says it talks to OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini and Qwen APIs as well as local models through Ollama or vLLM.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. The ==1.0 Preview, tagged on 11 November==, merges the agent harness of Alibaba's Qoder with Qwen Code and ships native packages for macOS, Linux and Windows without a separate Node.js install. A regular v0.27.3 release followed overnight, so this is a fast-moving, multi-provider alternative to vendor-locked coding agents.",
      "caveat": "The release notes say ==Preview interfaces, configuration and behaviour may change==. The main install path pipes a remote script into a shell, and model calls go to whichever provider or account you configure, with that provider's costs and data terms. We did not install or run it."
    },
