      ],
      "description": "TensorFold serves language models from a single Zig binary on Apple Silicon (Metal) and NVIDIA GPUs (CUDA). It reads checkpoints, tokenizes requests and runs its own kernels, and exposes OpenAI-style chat completions and Responses plus Anthropic Messages endpoints, with no Python or MLX install needed for serving.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. It is a rare from-scratch inference engine in Zig rather than a wrapper around llama.cpp or MLX, with ==one local server that speaks both OpenAI and Anthropic APIs==. Releases are frequent (v1.2.7 on 11 November), and the README documents pinned model revisions and checksum checks for its release archives.",
      "caveat": "GitHub's listing mentions Vulkan, but ==the README documents only Metal and CUDA== (CUDA 13, NVIDIA driver R580 or newer). The project is under five months old, its benchmarks are maintainer and community receipts rather than independent tests, model weights carry their own licenses, and its contributor tooling posts public check-ins to the maintainer's site."
    },
