      "description": "Free Claude Code is a local proxy that routes agent harnesses to other model providers. The README lists 12 clients, including Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Aider and VS Code Chat, and 61 providers, from free tiers such as NVIDIA NIM and OpenRouter to paid and local models, with retries, rate limits and provider fallback.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Despite the name, it does not hand out Anthropic's models: it ==keeps the Claude Code interface while swapping the model behind it==, which shows how interchangeable agent harnesses have become. It also adds Discord and Telegram front ends with voice notes.",
      "caveat": "The README states it is ==not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic==, and free-tier limits are set by each provider and may change; the 1.3B-free-tokens figure and up-to-90% token savings are maintainer claims. Your code and prompts go to the routed provider through API keys you store in this proxy. AGPL-3.0 applies (GitHub's API shows no detected license; the LICENSE file says AGPL-3.0-only)."
    },
