      "description": "llama.cpp is the widely used C/C++ engine for running LLMs locally, on CPUs and most GPU backends, with a command-line tool and an OpenAI-compatible llama-server. It is the base layer under many desktop model runners.",
      "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Its v0.9.0 release on 4 November adds ==FP8 E4M3 quantization and a flash-attention-rows op== for multi-sequence serving, four new model architectures including Mistral Large 4, and more speech models (Chatterbox TTS, Nemotron 3.5 Transcribe), plus ggml v0.29.0 with multi-node tensor parallelism.",
      "caveat": "It is a mature project, so Trending here reflects attention rather than a new launch. Speed depends heavily on your hardware, backend and quantization, and the ==quick-start installer pipes a remote script into a shell==; model weights come with their own licenses. We did not run it."
